 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "constraints",
  "visit": 1,
  "text": "I'm not done: the fixes are made but untested. The last two build attempts were refused because another Vivado job (PID 3553834) was already running, and the limit is one job at a time. The `check` tool also needs a synthesis result, so I couldn't run it either.\n\nI made two changes:\n- **FIFO memory type:** in `rtl/async_fifo.sv` I changed `FIFO_MEMORY_TYPE` from `\"block\"` to `\"distributed\"`. The earlier synthesis failed in the XPM CDC constraint step, which couldn't find the RAM clock pins on the block-RAM FIFO. I haven't confirmed that this is the cause. This change moves the 512\u00d732 memory out of block RAM, which spec.yaml expects (`bram36: 1`). That may affect the resource-range gate (`post_synth_resources_in_range`), and `architecture.yaml` may need revisiting.\n- **JTAG clock:** in `design.xdc` I added `create_clock -name jtag_tck -period 33.333` on `u_jtag/u_bscan/TCK` and put it in its own asynchronous clock group. This is aimed at the `post_synth_no_unconstrained_endpoints` failure, which listed 193 `u_jtag` registers with no clock. The 33.333 ns period (30 MHz) is my assumption for the JTAG clock, not a figure from the board files.\n\nThe first synthesis with only the FIFO change also failed the methodology, DRC, CDC-structure, exceptions and resource-range gates. I haven't looked into those yet.\n\nNext step: rerun `fda_build` with `until: synth` once the other job finishes, then run `fda_check` with `names: [\"all\"]` and read the remaining failures."
 },
